  "notes": "USAGE:\nMost commonly refers to romantic infidelity (sense 1). As a suru verb: {浮気|うわき}する (to cheat, to have an affair). As a na-adjective: {浮気|うわき}な{人|ひと} (a fickle/unfaithful person).\n\nThe compound {浮気|うわき}{性|しょう} describes someone who is habitually unfaithful or fickle by nature.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {浮気|うわき}する: to cheat, to have an affair\n- {浮気|うわき}がばれる: for cheating to be discovered\n- {浮気|うわき}{相手|あいて}: the person one is having an affair with\n- {浮気|うわき}{性|しょう}: fickle/unfaithful nature\n- {浮気|うわき}を{疑|うたが}う: to suspect infidelity",
